.TH LILI-CRASH 1 "September 2026" "lili-crash" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lili-crash \- find out why a program closed by itself
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lili-crash
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lili watches for programs that crash (systemd-coredump), a computer that froze, a Steam
game that closes right after starting, an app that exits with an error as it opens,
and errors recorded by Garuda's system updater.
She notifies each one and, with one click, opens an AI coding assistant (Claude Code,
Codex and others) in a terminal to find out why.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Programs that crashed, newest first, as JSON.
.TP
.BI mark " binary state" " \fR[\fIsummary\fR]"
Set a program to new, diagnosed, resolved or ignored.
.TP
.BI notify " id"
Show the notification for one crash (a PID), freeze (boot), Steam game (steam-...) or
app that didn't open (launch-...), or updater error (update-garuda-...).
.TP
.B watch
Notify every new event; the lili-crash user service runs this.
.TP
.B open
Lili's window: AI usage and crash history.
.TP
.BI diagnose " id" " \fR...\fR"
Open the AI in a terminal to find out why.
.TP
.BR config " [\fBset\fR \fIkey value\fR]"
Settings shared with the tray widget.
.TP
.BI install " agent"
Run an AI assistant's official installer in a terminal.
.TP
.BI package-open " file"
On Arch and its derivatives, identify a local .deb or .rpm and show a window with
the file, host system and intended installation. Install on this system opens the
configured AI with the lili-install-package skill for compatibility, native package
tracking, dependencies, icons and launchers. Cancel does not install anything.
Requires PySide6. Setup registers MIME openers once on Arch; arbitrary
terminal commands are not intercepted. Other distributions keep native openers.
.TP
.BR skill " \fBpath\fR|\fBview\fR|\fBedit\fR|\fBreset\fR"
This distribution's notes for the diagnosis skill.
.TP
.B setup
Per-user setup after installing a package: turns the service on, puts Lili in the
system tray and links the diagnosis skill for Claude and Codex.
.SH PREVENTION AND REPORTS
.TP
.B health
Print one read-only resource measurement. The service confirms sustained warnings
over three samples, without AI or automatic repairs.
.TP
.B config set preventive on|off
Enable or pause preventive monitoring of disk space, inodes, disk growth, memory
pressure and repeated kernel hardware/driver errors.
.TP
.B report export [file] [--days 30]
Export standardized incident metadata (1 to 365 days). No raw logs, hostnames,
paths or free-text diagnoses. Application identifiers remain. Without a filename,
print JSON. Existing files are never overwritten.
.TP
.B report save
Choose an export destination from the desktop.
.TP
.B report aggregate files... [--output file]
Compare exports locally across installations, group recurring symptoms and
deduplicate overlapping exports. No upload or central server is involved.
.PP
New settings default to Ollama with Linux-specific instructions, not newly trained
weights. Every remote session requires typing SEND before the agent starts. Initial
context is redacted on a best-effort basis; subsequent agent output is not filtered.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/lili/
Settings and your edited distribution notes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lili/
What you marked as diagnosed, resolved or ignored.
.TP
.I /var/log/garuda/garuda-update
Updater output, checked with its numbered rotations every 30 seconds. Explicit
error lines become events; arbitrary terminal output is not monitored.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/lili/updates.json
Saved updater error evidence and notification history (up to 100 events).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR coredumpctl (1),
https://github.com/cryptoconspiracy/lili-crash
